                    <h2 class="sub">                    Detachable-Capsule Pencil Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The Samson CL2 is a short, small-diaphragm condenser with interchangeable Omni and Cardioid capsules. It is sold as a stereo pair.</p><blockquote><p><cite>Tape Op - 2007</cite><br />I even used the CL2s to mic up a play at my son&#8217;s school, and I can say with confidence that the second and third-graders never sounded better. The parents all started using descriptives like &#8220;punchy&#8221; and &#8220;warm&#8221;. <br />Great little mics; a steal at $299 for the set.</p></blockquote><p><p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Samson/CL2">Samson CL2</a></p><p>The mic was released in 2006.</p>
